## Instrumentation refers to the process of adding code or using tools to collect telemetry data (such as logs, metrics, and traces) from an application.
## Automatic Instrumentation (or zero-code): Instrumentation is provided by OpenTelemetry agents or plugins not by modifying the code.
## Instrumentation Libraries (potentially code-based): require minimal code changes using libraries to instrument specific parts of an application where automatic methods may not reach or to extend it with custom logic.
## Manual Instrumentation (fully code-based): directly adding OpenTelemetry API calls in the source code.

